<article class="env-definition" id="040C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/040C">Definition <span data-tag="040C">18.32.6</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. The <em>Picard group</em> $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (\mathcal{O})$ of the ringed site is the abelian group whose elements are isomorphism classes of invertible $\mathcal{O}$-modules, with addition corresponding to tensor product. </p>
